---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="About SoloKit" description="SoloKit is a free set of private tools for freelancers working with clients around the world, made by Saif Siddiqui." current="about">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>About SoloKit</h1>
    <p class="lede">SoloKit is a free set of tools for the business side of freelancing: pricing, quoting, tracking time, invoicing, getting paid and following up.</p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>Most freelancers didn't go independent to do admin, yet pricing, paperwork and chasing payments eat hours every month. Many online tools ask for an account, add a watermark, or want your client data before they help. SoloKit gives you one clear tool for each step of a job, and the tools pass work to each other: an accepted quote becomes an invoice, tracked hours become invoice lines.</p>

    <h2>Your data stays with you</h2>
    <p>Every tool runs in your browser. What you type is not sent to a server, and there's no account to create. Your documents and settings are saved on your device so you can pick up where you left off, and you can download a backup or delete everything from your <a href={`${base}workspace/#data`}>Workspace</a>. The <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>privacy policy</a> has the details.</p>

    <h2>Who makes it</h2>
    <p>SoloKit is designed and built by <a href="https://saifi17.github.io">Saif Siddiqui</a>, an independent full-stack developer and UI/UX designer. Ideas for new tools and bug reports are welcome at <a href="mailto:saifsiddiqui1717@gmail.com">saifsiddiqui1717@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>A note on the numbers</h2>
    <p>The calculators give planning estimates, not tax, legal or financial advice. Tax rules and payment fees differ by country and change over time, so check important decisions with a qualified accountant and with your payment provider.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
